[al:新概念英语第一册]
[ti:A True Story]
[00:00.88]Lesson 119 | 第119课
[00:03.28]A true story | 一个真实的故事
[00:05.73]Listen to the tape then answer this question. | 听录音，然后回答这个问题。
[00:11.48]Who called out to the thieves in the dark? | 谁在黑暗中对窃贼叫喊？
[00:17.24]Do you like stories? | 你喜欢故事吗？
[00:20.90]I want to tell you a true story. | 我想给你讲一个真实的故事。
[00:24.96]It happened to a friend of mine a year ago. | 一年前，它发生在我的一位朋友身上。
[00:30.04]While my friend, George, was reading in bed, | 我的朋友乔治正在床上看书时，
[00:35.94]two thieves climbed into his kitchen. | 两个窃贼爬进了他的厨房。
[00:40.58]After they had entered the house, | 他们进入房子后，
[00:43.76]they went into the dining room. | 他们去了饭厅。
[00:47.32]It was very dark, so they turned on a torch. | 天很黑，所以他们打开了一个手电筒。
[00:54.41]Suddenly, they heard a voice behind them. | 突然，他们听到身后有个声音。
[00:59.28]'What's up? What's up?' someone called. | “怎么了？怎么了？”有人叫道。
[01:05.18]The thieves dropped the torch and ran away as quickly as they could. | 窃贼们扔下手电筒，尽可能快地跑走了。
[01:13.52]George heard the noise and came downstairs quickly. | 乔治听到响声，迅速下了楼。
[01:20.10]He turned on the light, but he couldn't see anyone. | 他打开灯，但没看到任何人。
[01:25.90]The thieves had already gone. | 窃贼们已经走了。
[01:29.93]But George's parrot, Henry, was still there. | 但乔治的鹦鹉亨利还在那儿。
[01:35.52]What's up, George? he called. | “怎么了，乔治？”它叫道。
[01:39.08]'Nothing, Henry,' George said and smiled. | “没什么，亨利，”乔治说着笑了。
[01:44.40]'Go back to sleep.' | “回去睡觉吧。”